    "body": "Looking at https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/parsing.html#speculative-fetch I agree this is a little bit weird, the whole thing is marked up with `<div algorithm>` but it's not an ordered list of steps. The use of \"let\" here seems weird.\r\n\r\nBut I think it's pretty clear what it's supposed to mean, and correctly referring to `<var>url</var>` makes it clearer.\r\n\r\nAs an alternative, I think this could just say:\r\n\r\n> When a URL is speculatively fetched, add that URL to the list of speculative fetch URLs.\r\n\r\nThoughts?",
    "created_at": "2026-01-15T13:46:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2026-01-15T13:46:26Z",
